.TH YOUR-GIT-IS-SHOWING 1 "July 2026" "v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
your-git-is-showing \- dump an exposed git repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B your-git-is-showing
[\fB\-b\fR \fIbranch\fR]
[\fB\-version\fR]
.I URL DIR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Your \fI.git\fR is showing!
.B your-git-is-showing
is a single-purpose tool that downloads an exposed Git repository served
over HTTP. Given a site URL, it fetches
.I .git
metadata (HEAD, refs, index, pack files, loose objects) and reconstructs the
repository locally. Enumerate a site to find the
.I .git,
or fire-and-forget and see what comes back.
.PP
.I URL
is the site root (or the directory containing the repo); the tool appends
.I /\.git
paths for you.
.I DIR
is the local directory where the reconstructed repo is written. On success
the tool sanitizes
.I .git/config
(commenting out
.I fsmonitor,
.I sshCommand,
.I askpass,
.I editor,
and
.I pager
entries) and runs
.BR "git checkout ."
to restore the working tree.
.PP
If
.I /\.git/
serves an HTML directory listing, the tool switches to recursive mode and
walks the listing; otherwise it uses targeted fetching of common files,
refs, pack files, and loose objects.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B 50 concurrent requests
.TP
.B 3 retries per request, 3s per-request timeout
.TP
.B Browser user-agent by default
.TP
.B Probes 10 common branch names by default
(main, master, staging, production, development, dev, develop, release, qa,
hotfix)
.TP
.B Recursive download of /\.git/
when the server exposes a directory listing
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " branch"
additional branch name to check for (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-version
print version and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B your-git-is-showing https://example.com/ myrepo
.TP
.B your-git-is-showing \-b develop https://example.com/repo/ repo-dump
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success — somebody's secrets just became yours
.TP
.B 1
dump failed
.TP
.B 2
invalid usage
.SH BUILD
.TP
.B go build .
.TP
.B go test ./...
.SH INSTALL
.TP
.B go install github.com/meta-byte/your-git-is-showing@latest
Requires Go 1.25+. Installs into
.I $GOPATH/bin.
Or build from source:
.TP
.B go build .
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B golang.org/x/net
(HTML parsing),
.B golang.org/x/sync
(bounded worker pool).
